{"tool_name":"microbiolink","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:microbiolink"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"MicrobioLink","home":"https://github.com/korcsmarosgroup/HMIpipeline","summary":"An integrated computational pipeline to infer functional effects of microbiome-host interactions.\n\nAbstract Microbiome-host interactions are important to nearly all living organisms, and play important roles in health and disease. Understanding these inter-kingdom cross-talks has a huge potential to advance diverse scientific domains such as the clinical and medical sciences, agriculture, and ecology. Detecting such interactions by experimental techniques remain challenging from a cost and feasibility perspective thus hampering large-scale analyses. Computational approaches not only make the inference of microbiome-host interactions viable but also scalable. Here, we present MicrobioLink, a computational pipeline to integrate predicted interactions between microbial and host proteins with host molecular networks.","addition_date":"2020-01-14T09:06:01Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:18:02.246630Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:MicrobioLink","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Pathway or network prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3439"},{"term":"Protein interaction prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2492"},{"term":"Virulence prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3461"}]}],"name":"MicrobioLink","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/837062","type":["Preprint"]},{"doi":"10.3390/cells9051278","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Agricultural science","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3810"},{"term":"Ecology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0610"},{"term":"Medical informatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3063"},{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Proteomics","u